        "original_id": "0c8b00bd-2135-5643-86e4-22d79cf559fa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Francis Ouimet, Jim Dale, Karen Valentine, Don Knotts, Jack Elam, Darren McGavin, Josh Flitter\n- Films: The Greatest Game Ever Played, Hot Lead and Cold Feet, Nancy Drew, Horton Hears a Who!\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Topics: biographical sports films, comedy-western films, acting roles, voice acting\n\nFacts:\n- The Greatest Game Ever Played is a 2005 biographical sports film based on the early life of golf champion Francis Ouimet.\n- Hot Lead and Cold Feet, originally titled Welcome to Bloodshy, is a 1978 American comedy-western film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- Hot Lead and Cold Feet stars Jim Dale, Karen Valentine, Don Knotts, Jack Elam, and Darren McGavin.\n- Josh Flitter played Eddie in The Greatest Game Ever Played.\n- Josh Flitter is known for playing Corky in Nancy Drew.\n- Josh Flitter voiced Rudy Kangaroo in the 2008 animated film Horton Hears a Who!.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
